-- title:
--   Original finite-range negative-mark SimpleFunc fibre sums reproduce physical marked counts and exact Lévy rate integrals
-- statement:
--   For every original source physical finite-activity Lévy process X and any nonpositive finite-range Borel simple function q_n on jump marks, choose jointly over countably many n finitely indexed physical negative-mark Poisson count representatives of each simple-function fibre. Construct measurable f_n, nonpositive almost surely, whose value is exactly the finite sum over the original actual nonzero jump times S of q_n(delta X_u), simultaneously for all n and every correct S. Construct r_n exactly equal to t times the original Lévy intensity integral exp(q_n)-1 and the corresponding finite disjoint negative Borel fibre intensity sum. The proof must use original physical jump-count a26 and source finite support and exact Borel Poisson law; no artificial independent marked process, and no pointwise limit assumptions or conclusion.
-- source:
